1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,480
When a payment page says paid, has any money moved?

2
00:00:03,530 --> 00:00:05,592
Picture a corner shop with a tab book.

3
00:00:05,642 --> 00:00:09,240
You take your bread, and the shopkeeper writes a line in the book.

4
00:00:09,290 --> 00:00:11,784
The money changes hands at the end of the week.

5
00:00:11,834 --> 00:00:13,848
A card payment works the same way.

6
00:00:13,898 --> 00:00:17,952
The page says paid in two seconds, but no money has moved yet.

7
00:00:18,002 --> 00:00:19,344
Two banks take part.

8
00:00:19,394 --> 00:00:23,544
The shop's bank is the acquirer, and this course builds its system.

9
00:00:23,594 --> 00:00:27,528
The buyer's bank is the issuer: it gave the buyer the card.

10
00:00:27,578 --> 00:00:33,528
When the buyer pays, the acquirer asks the issuer, through the card network, whether the payment is OK.

11
00:00:33,578 --> 00:00:38,952
The issuer checks the card and the money on the account, and says yes or no, in seconds.

12
00:00:39,002 --> 00:00:41,664
That yes is a line in the tab book, not money.

13
00:00:41,714 --> 00:00:47,592
The money moves later, in one batch for many payments, and that batch is called settlement.

14
00:00:47,642 --> 00:00:51,288
The acquirer keeps its fee and pays the shop the rest.

15
00:00:51,338 --> 00:00:55,968
Lesson 22 works out the fee, and Lesson 32 counts the day.

16
00:00:56,018 --> 00:00:58,200
Giving money back depends on timing.

17
00:00:58,250 --> 00:01:03,168
Before settlement, the line is simply crossed out, as if it never happened.

18
00:01:03,218 --> 00:01:06,048
No money has moved, so none has to move back.

19
00:01:06,098 --> 00:01:11,520
After settlement, the money has moved, so it has to be sent back, and that is a refund.

20
00:01:11,570 --> 00:01:15,504
Code that mixes the two loses money, or pays twice.

21
00:01:15,554 --> 00:01:17,472
So keep two pairs apart.

22
00:01:17,522 --> 00:01:19,104
Approved is not paid out.

23
00:01:19,154 --> 00:01:21,192
And cancelled is not refunded.

24
00:01:21,242 --> 00:01:23,040
Now find the tab book in the code.

25
00:01:23,090 --> 00:01:27,840
In the ecom repository, search the payment statuses for the words given back.

26
00:01:27,890 --> 00:01:29,712
Two statuses come back.

27
00:01:29,762 --> 00:01:35,616
The first is given back before settlement, as if it never happened, and its name is reversed.

28
00:01:35,666 --> 00:01:40,344
The second is given back after settlement, and its name is refunded.

29
00:01:40,394 --> 00:01:45,768
Approved is not paid out, and cancel is not refund: the tab book is in the code.

30
00:01:45,818 --> 00:01:48,096
Next: what you may keep about a card.
